omx-contract (2.15.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 2.15.0
  * debian/copyright: the vendored npm tarballs, MIT and BSD-3-Clause
  * codes: contract.descriptor.face-differs, the code an owner's face check
    raises
  * packaging: the omx-contract command in its own RPM
  * make install-cli: the omx-contract command, its vendored dependencies and
    its man page
  * vendor: the CLI's runtime dependencies as the npm tarballs
    package-lock.json pins
  * proof: the union of the contract and its owners against a tag's renders
  * data: eq, fbs, hrp, idelay and the DSP constants leave; the console rows
    go with them
  * data: the kernels and the hosting file leave for omx-dsp and omx-clap-core
  * docs: a host's continuous travels of a kernel live in
    primitives/<item>.json
  * contract-dir: two packages with a file of one kernel are refused
  * schema: a source link may carry its own at
  * validate: the EQ band budget skips a read that lacks one of its terms
  * schema: a descriptor control's symbol, beside its clap_id
  * links: an impl names its item by any C name the render spells for it
  * render: an owner's headers and module are framed by the render word in
    its own file
  * validate: every leaf of every sheet resolves to a finite number
  * schema: the plugin descriptor words, their rules and their refusal codes
  * docs: the plugin descriptor words, the three origins and their refusal
    codes
  * ci: install the data as the contract directory, render it back, check the
    links
  * The contract directory reader, its refusal codes as data, and the links
    check
  * schema: x-omx-schema-version, and the requires and source words a
    definition file carries
  * docs: the contract directory, its manifest, the requires and source words
    and the reader's refusal codes

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:29:38 +0000
